# .cursorrules — orientation for Cursor when editing this repository

This is a portable AI coding agent skill pack, not a runnable application. Zero runtime dependencies.

## Before editing

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/SKILL_CONTRACT.md`, and `docs/RUNTIME_INTEGRATION.md`.
2. Run `npm test && npm run validate`. Both must pass before any commit.

## Skill content standard

Every `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` MUST contain:
- YAML frontmatter: `name:` (matches directory), `description: Use when ...` (searchable)
- Sections: `## Purpose`, `## Activate when`, `## Repository inspection`, `## Decision rules`, `## Implementation procedure`, `## Failure modes`, `## Verification`
- ≤ 500 lines
- Anchor skills (most-routed) should be ≥ 100 lines with commands, library names, and code samples

## Runtime files

- `lib/skill-loader.mjs` — prompt routing + adapter detection
- `lib/mcp-server.mjs` — MCP server (stdio, JSON-RPC 2.0)
- `bin/skills.mjs` — CLI
- `lib/routing-evaluator.mjs` — deterministic routing regression harness

## Adding a skill

1. Create `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` following the content standard.
2. Register in `skill-manifest.yml` under `skills:` with `name`, `category`, `triggers: [...]`.
3. Add a routing case to `router/ROUTING_CASES.yml` (primary + secondary).
4. Add an evaluation case to the relevant `evals/cases/<workflow>/workflow.yml`.
5. Run `npm test && npm run validate`.

## Commit rules

- No `Co-Authored-By` trailers.
- Each commit must keep CI green (`npm test && npm run validate`).
